  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Organic compound is heated with fuming nitric acid in the presence of silver nitrate in carius method. Lunar caustic <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced></math> is used as reagent hare to distinguish <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>Br</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math> respectively as follows.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mover><mi>AgCl</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8595;</mo><mi>ppt</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;white</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Br</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mover><mi>AgBr</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8595;</mo><mi>ppt</mi></msub></math> pale yellow</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mover><mi>AgI</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8595;</mo><mi>ppt</mi></msub></math> Dark yellow</p>",
